truction of personal data through the incident-management process.\",\n          \"operational timelines. 5. Data Sharing and Third Parties Personal data may be shared with service providers that perform functions such as hosting, payment processing, customer support, analytics, security, or communications. Third-party processors should receive only the information reasonably necessary for the contracted service and should be subject to confidentiality, security, and data-protection obligations. 6. Data Retention For this academic case study, customer account and transaction records are normally retained for 5 years after the end of the customer relationship, unless a shorter period is required by an applicable rule or the data is no longer necessary. When retention is no longer required, personal data should be securely deleted, anonymized, or otherwise rendered non-identifiable where appropriate. 7. Personal Data Breach Response The Company will maintain procedures for detecting, assessing, containing, documenting, and responding to personal-data breaches.\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# ============================================================\n","# STEP 13: PROCESS ALL PRIVACY DOCUMENTS\n","# ============================================================\n","all_chunks=[]\n","for p in DOC_FILES: all_chunks.extend(create_document_chunks(p))\n","print('Documents processed:',len(DOC_FILES)); print('Total chunks:',len(all_chunks))\n","display(pd.DataFrame(all_chunks).head(5))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"41ba3622","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":485,"referenced_widgets":["f407ff65108b447c966623baf7736c0e","3b3ef4e43b4b4ab591a25c654b97ffc8","8a56871ec39f4c638203963979a06585","e64c5317e4c347cc8b3fd569106f421f","ee080860354b4441a65edf618bad5935","e6fd9facb7c24856af657b1343d1af1e","cfab5e56382c42bc8c4f80a1f0572